{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 final classification (2026-08-17)\n\nProblem: live Jira DC scenario 9 fails when its explicit `git commit` exits 1 with `nothing to commit, working tree clean` after `bridge_projects_set`.\n\nProven mechanism: the scenario retains an August 14 workaround at `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py:664-679` that manually commits `.bridge_state/projects.json`. Commit `c601fe739f` (August 15; closed/signed ticket `cubiform-wooden-fruitbat`) deliberately changed `bridge_projects_set` so its read-modify-write runs under `write_lock` and then calls `commit_and_push_tickets_branch` (`src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:110-128`). The setter therefore commits the mapping first; the scenario’s later commit is redundant and Git correctly returns 1 for a clean tree. Jira state is not causal.\n\nDiscriminating proof: the same isolated local-Git probe was run on the exact historical boundary with `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off`. At `c601fe739f^`, `bridge_projects_set` did NOT advance HEAD, left `M .bridge_state/projects.json`, and the manual commit returned 0. At `c601fe739f`, the setter advanced HEAD, left porcelain status empty, and the manual commit returned 1 with `nothing to commit, working tree clean`. On current main, the runtime seam guard `test_mutation_runs_under_write_lock_and_publishes` passes, and a real-Git probe advances HEAD with subject `bridge: update projects mapping` and leaves the tree clean. This rules out wrong-path/no-op writes, fixture/ensure side effects, Jira drift, and flakiness.\n\nClassification: `intended-behavior` for the product; the CI failure is a stale harness expectation. Authoritative contract: `docs/concurrency.md:668-684` mandates that EVERY tickets-branch mutation auto-commit+auto-publish and explicitly names `.bridge_state/projects.json` plus `bridge_projects_set/remove`; `docs/config.md:338-342` and `docs/user-guide.md:494-501` call the mapping committed tickets-branch state; closed ticket `cubiform-wooden-fruitbat` and commit `c601fe739f` deliberately introduced this behavior and added the executable regression guard. The originating story `gasolinic-microbian-puffin` had called the former uncommitted behavior a latent durability seam. Reverting production would violate the invariant and recreate that durability defect.\n\nRecommended non-fix disposition (awaiting grouped user decision per policy): preserve product auto-commit semantics; remove the stale manual add/commit block and replace it with a harness precondition asserting `HEAD:.bridge_state/projects.json` exists and the path is clean before `run_ensures`. Strengthen the non-external real-Git library contract test to assert the setter advances tracker HEAD, the mapping is present in HEAD, and porcelain status for the path is empty. No production or test files were changed in this investigation.\n\nProtocol disposition: Phase 2 not entered because the not-a-bug guard classified the alleged product behavior as intended. RED/GREEN, mutation, caller/parity/sibling repair sweeps, and live replication are therefore not applicable until the user approves the test-contract alignment. Residual risk: the stale live-only harness remains red; disposition is this blocked decision item."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787031287485057001,"uuid":"449733a4-45cd-47d3-a624-ccc1aae8edce"}